      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_30",
      "quote": "DA appears safe and may alleviate GP consultation workload, supporting more rational imaging and prescribing [32-36, 38]. For France, scaling would require structured triage/protocols [20, 22, 23], interoperable tools, explicit collaboration frameworks [15, 16], and training in differential diagnosis for physiotherapists [49]; evaluation within community health centres could monitor real-world impact [21, 53, 54]. Beyond clinical safety, implementation should be viewed as a reconfiguration of care pathways, with implications for professional roles, accountability, and continuity of care in primary care teams. Embedding DA within coordinated organisational models may therefore be as critical as regulatory change to ensure sustainable adoption.",
